# Suppressions for Docker image scans (backend + database migration images).
# Everything below lives in the node:24-alpine base's bundled npm CLI
# (usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules), which the containers never
# invoke: they only run `node dist/...`. Not fixable via pnpm overrides; each
# clears once the base bundles an npm with the fixed version.
#
# Do NOT merge into the root .trivyignore: that one is read by the dependency
# scan of our own lockfile, which must keep catching these CVEs in app code.

# undici@6.26.0, WebSocket DoS. npm opens no WebSockets. Fixed in 6.27.0.
CVE-2026-12151

# brace-expansion@5.0.6 ReDoS/DoS, three CVE ids for the same copy.
# Fixed in 5.0.7 / 5.0.8 / 5.0.9. App tree resolves >= 5.0.9.
CVE-2026-13149
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152

# tar@7.5.16 DoS via crafted archives. npm never extracts untrusted archives
# here. Fixed in 7.5.19.
CVE-2026-59873
CVE-2026-59874

# ip-address@10.2.0 (via socks) octet-parsing confusion. No SOCKS proxying.
# Fixed in 10.3.1. Not in our lockfile at all.
CVE-2026-69192
